.TH PERSO_NATIVE 9 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Kernel Developer's Manual"
.SH NAME
perso_native \- Native Substrate kernel personality
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/exec/perso/personality.h>
.PP
.BI "extern struct personality " personality_native ";"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B perso_native
personality implements the canonical system call interface for the Substrate operating system. It allows native applications (compiled specifically for this kernel) to interact with the hardware and kernel services.
.PP
This personality uses the Reference Syscall Table, which is largely inspired by standard Unix System V and Linux numbering but may diverge for new, custom features.
.SH SYSCALLS
Key system calls implemented in the native personality include:
.TP
.B SYS_EXIT (1)
Terminate the current process.
.TP
.B SYS_FORK (2)
Create a new process.
.TP
.B SYS_READ (3)
Read from a file descriptor.
.TP
.B SYS_WRITE (4)
Write to a file descriptor.
.TP
.B SYS_OPEN (5)
Open and possibly create a file.
.TP
.B SYS_CLOSE (6)
Close a file descriptor.
.TP
.B SYS_TIME (13)
Get time of day (seconds since epoch).
.TP
.B SYS_MKNOD (14)
Create a filesystem node (special file).
.TP
.B SYS_GET_COW_STATS (241)
Custom debugging syscall to retrieve Copy-On-Write statistics for the memory manager.
.SH EXTENSIONS
The native personality is the designated host for all Kernel Virtual Machine (KVM) API extensions, including process introspection (`sys_proc_*`) and system statistics (`sys_vm_*`), as detailed in the project roadmap.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR personality (9),
.BR perso_linux (9)
